  ! White: registered is 154% of the level above it. ⛔ THE RATIO IS IMPOSSIBLE; THE COUNT IS NOT. Registration and votes are administrative events — an in-person appearance with an ID book — and the denominator is a MODELLED small-area census estimate, so the term that fails here is the estimate. The published ward totals are untouched either way: this machinery SPLITS them and does not revise them, so what a ratio above 1 impeaches is the split, not the roll. Do NOT read this as a census UNDERCOUNT either: the published Census 2022 figures for the white and Indian groups are argued to be too HIGH, not too low (over-adjustment for a 62%/72% post-enumeration undercount, leaving them 14%/24% above projections), which makes this gap wider rather than narrower. See DATA-QUALITY.md item 11.
